If so,
these pairwise joint distributions should satisfy the following inequality,
abbreviated CHSH (Clauser, Horne, Shimony, \& Holt, 1969; Fine, 1982):
\begin{equation}
\max_{k,l\in\left\{ 1,2\right\} }\left|\sum_{i,j\in\left\{ 1,2\right\} }\mathsf{E}\left[A_{i}B_{j}\right]-2\mathsf{E}\left[A_{k}B_{l}\right]\right|-2\leq0,\label{eq: CHSH}
\end{equation}
where $\mathsf{E}$ is expected value.

\begin{equation}
\max_{k,l\in\left\{ 1,2\right\} }\left|\sum_{i,j\in\left\{ 1,2\right\} }\mathsf{E}\left[A_{i}B_{j}\right]-2\mathsf{E}\left[A_{k}B_{l}\right]\right|-2\leq0,\label{eq: CHSH}
\end{equation}

